{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"14894802298e74a5","type":"text","text":"The idea that Sara would have went home if she'd had one so she thinks she understands that Savanna will come back because this is home. This is her family, she'll come back to family because it's family, it's where she belongs and is accepted no matter what is what. At least that's what Sara thinks. Also, Sara thinks Savanna is just saying things she doesn't mean in anger, like Sara herself did many many times at that age and has struggled to not do for years now. ","x":220,"y":-58,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"34c96adedb29ad7d","type":"text","text":"Again, how could she even ask that? Sara was capable of many things that she would never do to any of them.","x":-434,"y":-169,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"503fdcd15d9d76cd","x":760,"y":-120,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"<!-- \"I don't know why you have to even ask, but we would never do that to you or your sisters.\"  -->\n\n\n\n<!-- \"How can you even ask that?\" - \"How? I told you, I watched Sara do it to strangers.\"  -->\n\n\n\n<!-- I'm sick of all this weird shit you make me pretend is perfectly fine.\"  -->"}
	],
